<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The launcher icon's front layer — the app's own brand mark.

    It points straight at `auth_logo`, the torus the splash and both auth screens already draw, rather
    than at a copy: one mark, one file, and 114 kB that the APK was carrying anyway. The source is a
    309 x 321 4x export, so the largest bucket a launcher asks for (108dp at xxxhdpi = 432px, of which
    the mark is 256px) is still a downscale — it never has to invent pixels.

    Sized explicitly because the asset lives in `drawable-nodpi`: with no density scaling, its intrinsic
    size is 309 *device* pixels on every phone, which would overflow an mdpi 108px canvas threefold and
    under-fill an xxxhdpi one. 64 x 66.5dp is Figma's own 1.039 aspect kept intact, centred in the
    108dp layer — so the mark sits inside the 72dp region Android guarantees every mask leaves visible,
    with 4dp of air to spare on the widest side.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item
        android:width="64dp"
        android:height="66.5dp"
        android:drawable="@drawable/auth_logo"
        android:gravity="center" />
</layer-list>
